learning_outcomes:
  - Recognise when the Computer Misuse Act 1990 applies to a scenario, including scenarios where another Act might appear to apply at first glance
  - Identify which section of the Act has been engaged (s1, s2, s3, s3ZA or s3A) and explain the difference between them
  - Define what "unauthorised access" means under the Act, including the task-specific nature of authorisation
  - Recognise that the Act is technology-agnostic and applies to any computer system regardless of device type
prerequisites: []
estimated_minutes: 30
last_reviewed: 2026-05-16
revision_notes: |
  2026-05-15: Initial draft. Second Paper 1 topic in CA 4.1 (Inc 5.1).
  Drill, MCQ and NEI calibrated against the Paper 1 legislation-recognition
  pattern. MCQ uses a dual-Act distractor (DPA) to drill the recognition
  step at the boundary where most students slip.
  2026-05-16: Inc 7.1 cyberpunk-comic conversion. Prose body replaced
  with six panels and a closer using the Inc 7.0 comic-* Markdoc tags.
